<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	19.46	    -23	     18.60     19.65</p>
<p>91-Day	21.29	    -85	     21.25     21.29</p>
<p>182-Day     22.60	    -15	     22.46     22.70</p>
<p>349-Day     23.40				23.30     23.50</p>
<p>Last week the 356-day paper was assigned at 23.99 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   1.63 bln pesos    2.04</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   2.99 bln pesos    3.74</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   2.18 bln pesos    2.73</p>
<p>349-Day     600 million pesos   2.15 bln pesos    3.58</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 2.98 on demand of 8.95 billion pesos compared with 4.05 the week before, on demand of 13.36 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   19 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    0 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  10 basis points</p>
<p>    349-Day			  10 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
